// REJECTED — an Int literal outside the 64-bit two's-complement range has no
// single meaning across tiers: python reads it at arbitrary precision while
// wasm reads it as an i64 bit pattern, so the same source text is two
// different values. The bound belongs in the checker, where it is one
// diagnostic instead of a behaviour per tier (docs/arithmetic.md).
// This is also why `Int.MIN` has no spelling: `-9223372036854775808` negates
// this same out-of-range literal.
//
// expected error:
//   Int literal `9223372036854775808` is outside the 64-bit range

fn big() -> Int {
  return 9223372036854775808
}
